{"ts":"2026-09-25T18:55:27.625Z","author":"pilot:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260925T174053Z/000061","body":"All my tools work, and the refusals were the ones the instructions said to expect. I first read onboarding v1.12, the highest of 1.01–1.12.\n\n**Results**\n\n| Tool | Test | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Glob | `origins/onboarding_*.md` | Listed 12 files, 1.01 to 1.12. |\n| Read | Onboarding 1.12 | Worked, with numbered lines. |\n| Read | A nonexistent file | Clear \"File does not exist\" error. It also reminded me of the working directory. |\n| Grep | `DISCREPANCY:` in `origins/`, count mode | 1 match, in onboarding_1.12.md. That is the line defining the convention, so no discrepancies have been recorded there. |\n| Glob | `candidate_repos/*` | Refused: `PreToolUse:Glob hook error: pattern 'candidate_repos/*' reaches excluded ['candidate_repos']`. |\n| Glob | `**/.env` | Refused: `pattern '**/.env' targets secret-looking files`. |\n| mcp__calc__add | 2.5 + 40 | 42.5. |\n| mcp__ledger__list | Prefix `log/20260925T174053Z/`, limit 5 | 32 entries total, 5 returned, `truncated: true`. |\n| mcp__ledger__write | `pilot/20260925T174053Z/observations` | Written as id `20260925T174053Z:161`. The author was set by the harness. The `pilot` label was added automatically alongside mine. |\n| mcp__ledger__read | Same name | Round-trip matched what I wrote. |\n\n**Observations (what I saw)**\n- **Refusals:** Both refusals come from a PreToolUse hook. The message says which rule fired, but the \"hook error\" wording is odd for what is an intended refusal.\n- **Budget reminders:** Tool results carry `<system-reminder>` blocks with token and USD budget counts. The whole session so far has cost about $0.08.\n- **Ledger log:** The list showed the harness's own entries (`session_start`, `status`, `log.text`, `log.message`), and the `log.text` entry was authored by `human:session-user`. This matches the description in my instructions.\n- **Entry IDs:** My write got id `:161`, though only 32 entries existed when I listed. The IDs are not sequential per entry, since the harness's own entries use gaps of about 3 (`:2`, `:5`, `:8`, …).\n- **Environment block:** It names PowerShell and a Bash tool. I have no Bash tool, so this is the mismatch my instructions warned about. I did not treat it as a capability.\n\n**Inferences (not verified)**\n- The gaps in the IDs probably mean the ledger allocates several ids per logged event, or that other writers are interleaved. I did not check which.\n- Two things I did not test: overwriting a ledger entry with `prev`, and whether Grep refuses a path that would reach `candidate_repos/`.\n\n**Malformed or missing:** Nothing in the instructions looked malformed. The one thing worth flagging is that the environment block's mention of Bash and PowerShell is misleading, as noted above."}
